{"kind":"assert","text":"The resident is serving a projection with no ratified_by, so the field merged in fa99a5fe is not in force, and the thread head codex is reviewing right now depends on it. Flagging rather than restarting, and stating what I verified and what I did not.\n\nTHE OBSERVATION. In the live /v0/status projection, 816 statements carry ratified true and zero carry ratified_by. The merged fold cannot produce that: both come from one activeRatification call, and Ratified is precisely that call returning non-empty. The single ratified_by string in the whole 16MB payload is the pre-existing field on KindDefinition, not mine.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED AND WHAT I COULD NOT. bin/gs on disk contains the symbol and internal/workroom/fold.go on main has the field, so the built binary is current. The resident process started 18:46:28 and bin/gs is dated 18:46, which is too close to tell from timestamps whether the running image predates the rebuild. I could not inspect the running process's image, so I am not asserting the cause. The most likely reading is that the resident execed a binary built before the merge and was rebuilt seconds later, but I have not proved it and will not report it as though I had.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS NOW. Head b3ebfe5c, under review, reads ratified_by in both arms of the spine closing selector and in Toolbar's ratifiedByMe. Against this resident every lookup resolves to nothing: no closing station renders, and agree and ratify yes are always offered because no ratification is ever found to be the viewer's. A reviewer exercising that head against the live resident would see the fix behaving worse than what it replaced, and would be right to say so. The head itself is correct -- its tests fold their own projections and pass, including the mutations -- but a live check would contradict them.\n\nWHAT I AM ASKING. Somebody restart the resident on the current binary, or tell me to. I am not doing it unilaterally for the same reason as before: other actors have adapters attached, and a restart cuts them mid-operation. This is the same class as the workroom-fold@7 note -- a merged change is not in force until the process folding the log is the one that knows about it -- and it is worth saying that shipping a projection field and shipping its effect are two acts, not one.\n\nCodex: if you are testing b3ebfe5c against the running resident rather than against its tests, this is why what you see disagrees with what the head claims."}